{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra","id":1488772,"title":"The true potential of the Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-02T01:07:07-07:00","id":1488772,"title":"The true potential of the Umbra","content":"I'll begin with a question for the ST and the players from older version too, what exactly have umbral reflection? The book say that everything that exist for long enough or with a particular spiritual importance in the physical world get a reflexion, without saying if it concern only material things or also idea, concept etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T02:34:49-07:00","id":1488777,"title":"","content":"There are spirits tied to ideas and concepts.<br /> <br /> Generally I think the umbra-landscape is also tied to concepts and ideas relevant to the place in question. Such are reflected in the general descriptions, rather than with particular spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T03:41:54-07:00","id":1488782,"title":"","content":"Umbral geography gets a bit complicated with which reflections go where. As a rule of thumb, abstract concepts (Love, Knowledge, Mathematics..) tend to be reflected in the High Umbra, while concepts and ideas with a material representation get reflected either in the Middle Umbra or as Zones or Realms. For example, the Digital Web is the spiritual reflection of the physical digital communication network - but also of the concept of such networking - and exists as a Zone that touches all Umbrae. The CyberRealm is a Near Realm within the Middle Umbra that exists as a reflection of the Weaver aspect within humanity cranked up to 11. Highly localized concepts tend to get represented as a Spirit.<br /> <br /> Further complicating the issue is that something could easily be represented in the High Umbra as an abstraction, as a Realm or Zone, and Spirit all at once. Luna exists as a Celestine, a place in the Middle Umbra, and probably as many times as an abstract concept in the High Umbra as someone used the Moon as a metaphor.<br /> <br /> This applies to prominent places, too. You can visit an iteration of the Library of Alexandria in each of the Umbrae, and probably the Dreaming as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-02-2022, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T04:38:22-07:00","id":1488793,"title":"","content":"So basically, depending on the nature of the physical thing, it will appear to specifics area in the umbra. Knowing this we all agree that the more powerfull is the idea or the influence of the physicall thing, the more chance it got to appear. We know that the sun and the moon, even if not worshipped by whole world have a spiritual reflection as Helios and Luna.<br /> <br /> So the same way, gravity, time, light, darkness etc... may have very powerfull reflection and maybe incarnation in the umbra. And by extension they have their lower spirits wich can interact with other beings, the garou in that case.<br /> <br /> We also know from the book on the umbra that some spirit are born from human creation, i think about the incarna of dollar<br /> <br /> As humans creationss can be reflected in the umbra is there a limit? Cause some famous idea or concept, let's say star wars universe, could be be reflected somewhere in the umbra.<br /> Is there a limitation that avoid a glass walker pack to look for that place and pick up lightsabers before going back in the physical world? I would like to avoid having my pc's telling me &quot;we're going to look for Luke Skywalker and get the Force gift&quot;:/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 08-02-2022, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T04:46:56-07:00","id":1488799,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> is right. However, as far as I recall WtA doesn't go into detail about umbra types. The High Umbra, Middle Umbra and Low Umbra classification is a MtA thing, iirc.<br /> <br /> And sure, while concepts like Love, Knowledge and Mathematics would fall into the purview of the High Umbra, or Astralplane, there are middle Umbra (the Umbra that counts for WtA mostly) spirits that have aspects of Love (like Unicorn) or Knowledge (Owl, Uktena) and so on.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd interpret Umbral descriptions as a matter how far removed an area is from the physical world. Penumbra being the closest, then Near Umbra (including its Realms, Domains and Subdomains) and then the Deep or Far Umbra. The Penumbra is the most direct reflection of a concrete thing or concept. The love and Caring Foster parents have for the children the raise is concretely reflected in their house's penumbra reflection. It is probably a warm and light and beautiful place. The soul of the place, so to speak. This might also be reflected in the sprits that reside there, if any.<br /> The Astral Plane (High Umbra) also has a layer that is close to the physical world. Auspex 5 leads there, for example. But it is said to reflect one's own inner psyche in regards to things. So if the visitor has had bad experiences in the Foster Care, the place might be frightful for him, but not for another visitor who has a neutral outlook on the matter of foster care.<br /> <br /> But Garou rarely are in the Astral Plane, unless they employ 1st Edition Stargazer Gifts, iirc. Or they undertake long journeys into the far umbra reaches, where they might cross over between middle Umbra, High Umbra, Dark Umbra or Dreaming.<br /> <br /> At least that is my take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T05:42:19-07:00","id":1488806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488793#post1488793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically, depending on the nature of the physical thing, it will appear to specifics area in the umbra. Knowing this we all agree that the more powerfull is the idea or the influence of the physicall thing, the more chance it got to appear. We know that the sun and the moon, even if not worshipped by whole world have a spiritual reflection as Helios and Luna.<br /> <br /> So the same way, gravity, time, light, darkness etc... may have very powerfull reflection and maybe incarnation in the umbra. And by extension they have their lower spirits wich can interact with other beings, the garou in that case.<br /> <br /> We also know from the book on the umbra that some spirit are born from human creation, i think about the incarna of dollar<br /> <br /> As humans creationss can be reflected in the umbra is there a limit? Cause some famous idea or concept, let's say star wars universe, could be be reflected somewhere in the umbra.<br /> Is there a limitation that avoid a glass walker pack to look for that place and pick up lightsabers before going back in the physical world? I would like to avoid having my pc's telling me &amp;quot;we're going to look for Luke Skywalker and get the Force gift&amp;quot;:/</div> </div> </div> </div>Particularly in the Dreaming is where you would find most of those... Things. Luke's lightsaber is probably the least of your concerns; you could try to snach Sauron's One Ring (althought that may not be the best of the ideas come to think about it), or Gabriel Anchangel's flamming sword, or try to &quot;recruit&quot; Superman...<br /> <br /> The one thing thou, all of those are spirits, and cant normally cross the Gauntlet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T06:01:56-07:00","id":1488809,"title":"","content":"There is the TV subdomain, where movies and TV shows might be real.<br /> Also, it is said, that the tribe that eventually became the Glass Walkers got distracted from their duty to warden the humans in the cities (you know protect them from themselves and supernatural influences) by the realisation that humans created things which lead to new spirits emerging. Some even arrived at levels, where they can create jagglings to serve as totem avatars to packs like the American Dream or the Mighty Dollar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T06:05:32-07:00","id":1488810,"title":"","content":"The Umbra has also metaphysical failsafes in place. Certain things only work within the immediate context of the Umbral realm they are native to, the Rules of Near Realms being the most prominent example. The lightsaber might only work within the metaphysics of the Star Wars Canon bubble of the Umbra, the Son of Krypton would lose all his powers once he steps out of his private umbral universe (better get Batman).<br /> <br /> There are so many concepts that involve the End of All Things as We Know Them which have an umbral reflection, yet neither the Umbra nor the material world has been run over by sentient nano von Neumann machines, devoured by False Vacuum Decay, or invaded by the Zerg. Because each of their realms has their own rules that don't apply to others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T06:30:25-07:00","id":1488814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488810#post1488810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Umbra has also metaphysical failsafes in place. Certain things only work within the immediate context of the Umbral realm they are native to, the Rules of Near Realms being the most prominent example. The lightsaber might only work within the metaphysics of the Star Wars Canon bubble of the Umbra, the Son of Krypton would lose all his powers once he steps out of his private umbral universe (better get Batman).<br /> <br /> There are so many concepts that involve the End of All Things as We Know Them which have an umbral reflection, yet neither the Umbra nor the material world has been run over by sentient nano von Neumann machines, devoured by False Vacuum Decay, or invaded by the Zerg. Because each of their realms has their own rules that don't apply to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a pitty frankly, 'cuz I would love to borrow a few magic holes from the Looney Tunes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T08:36:53-07:00","id":1488828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488810#post1488810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Umbra has also metaphysical failsafes in place. Certain things only work within the immediate context of the Umbral realm they are native to, the Rules of Near Realms being the most prominent example. The lightsaber might only work within the metaphysics of the Star Wars Canon bubble of the Umbra, the Son of Krypton would lose all his powers once he steps out of his private umbral universe (better get Batman).<br /> <br /> There are so many concepts that involve the End of All Things as We Know Them which have an umbral reflection, yet neither the Umbra nor the material world has been run over by sentient nano von Neumann machines, devoured by False Vacuum Decay, or invaded by the Zerg. Because each of their realms has their own rules that don't apply to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>That fact that if those spirit leave their realm they loose their powers, are you sure about this? Cause spirit use charm and to my knowledge they still can use them while in physical world. However object like lightsabers and harry potter wand would obviously lose all their supernatural ability out of their home realm. On the other hand spirits cans teach gifts to Garou, i'm curious on what would give a jedi gift on a garou","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T09:01:06-07:00","id":1488832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488828#post1488828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That fact that if those spirit leave their realm they loose their powers, are you sure about this? Cause spirit use charm and to my knowledge they still can use them while in physical world. However object like lightsabers and harry potter wand would obviously lose all their supernatural ability out of their home realm. On the other hand spirits cans teach gifts to Garou, i'm curious on what would give a jedi gift on a garou</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the spirit. The spirits that are integral parts of a realm are tiny and defined by the realm, they can easily dissapate and lose power they are further away from the realm they make up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T09:04:42-07:00","id":1488833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488828#post1488828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That fact that if those spirit leave their realm they loose their powers, are you sure about this? Cause spirit use charm and to my knowledge they still can use them while in physical world. However object like lightsabers and harry potter wand would obviously lose all their supernatural ability out of their home realm. On the other hand spirits cans teach gifts to Garou, i'm curious on what would give a jedi gift on a garou</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on the type of Spirit. Most Spirits that inhabit a Realm are Emanations, a special type of Spirit that is created as part of the Realm itself. Technically, anything created within a Realm is an Emanation, including objects. While the Emanation of Superman may have super powers within its Realm, it does not have Charms or work at all like the Spirits you would encounter in the Spirit Wilds. A Luke Skywalker Emanation can't teach you to use the Force, at least not for outside its umbral bubble.<br /> <br /> If it helps, think of umbral Realms as Star Trek holodecks with the safety turned off. Emanations are everything the holodeck creates for its simulation. Once you change the simulation (step into another Realm, Zone, or the Penumbra), the rules change and anything you take with you has to follow those new rules. Once you leave the holodeck (cross the Gauntlet), stuff vanishes.<br /> <br /> I think there are certain Arts for Changelings that allow them to take things out of the Dreaming into the material world, but I'm pretty sure it's not that easy for Shapechangers. At least I can't think of a Gift on top of my head that would allow this.<br /> <br /> Rarely, there are physical objects that somehow found their way into umbral Realms and can be brought back. These tend to be fetishes or magic materials and are meant as quest goals- Pathstones are a good example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-02-2022, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T10:07:05-07:00","id":1488845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra#post1488772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book say that everything that exist for long enough or with a particular spiritual importance in the physical world get a reflexion,</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda funny, if you think about it, the Universe is 13.77 billion years old (plus or minus 40 million years)... so if anything, the Universe should have the oldest refelction, not to mention a really big one. And probably the oldest Spirit...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T10:26:37-07:00","id":1488847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488833#post1488833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends on the type of Spirit. Most Spirits that inhabit a Realm are Emanations, a special type of Spirit that is created as part of the Realm itself. Technically, anything created within a Realm is an Emanation, including objects. While the Emanation of Superman may have super powers within its Realm, it does not have Charms or work at all like the Spirits you would encounter in the Spirit Wilds. A Luke Skywalker Emanation can't teach you to use the Force, at least not for outside its umbral bubble.<br /> <br /> If it helps, think of umbral Realms as Star Trek holodecks with the safety turned off. Emanations are everything the holodeck creates for its simulation. Once you change the simulation (step into another Realm, Zone, or the Penumbra), the rules change and anything you take with you has to follow those new rules. Once you leave the holodeck (cross the Gauntlet), stuff vanishes.<br /> <br /> I think there are certain Arts for Changelings that allow them to take things out of the Dreaming into the material world, but I'm pretty sure it's not that easy for Shapechangers. At least I can't think of a Gift on top of my head that would allow this.<br /> <br /> Rarely, there are physical objects that somehow found their way into umbral Realms and can be brought back. These tend to be fetishes or magic materials and are meant as quest goals- Pathstones are a good example.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Learn how to use the force natively would work only in that realm of course i agree but are you saying that if those spirits teach garou their gift they would only work in their realm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T10:30:27-07:00","id":1488849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488845#post1488845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda funny, if you think about it, the Universe is 13.77 billion years old (plus or minus 40 million years)... so if anything, the Universe should have the oldest refelction, not to mention a really big one. And probably the oldest Spirit...</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite possible it might exist. It's not featured in Werewolf by name, but as a concept it most likely has a quite ancient Spirit, one made when the universe was both flesh and spirit as one. I cannot imagine it liking being split in two by the cosmic principles of the Triat, but the focus of Werewolf is this particular slice of the universe around Gaia.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T10:35:30-07:00","id":1488851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488847#post1488847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Learn how to use the force natively would work only in that realm of course i agree but are you saying that if those spirits teach garou their gift they would only work in their realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gifts are not related to the Spirits once they are taught to the Garou, they become a part of them and who they are powered by the Garou's spiritual self. So if you were taught a Gift you would keep it, however not all Spirits are capable of teaching you Gifts - most emanations wouldn't be, as they are minor spirits of low cosmic power.<br /> <br /> For instance, if you went into the TV zone and met a cartoon bear, that cartoon bear would be unlikely to be able to teach you any bear gifts or cartoon gifts. On the other hand if you met Bugs Bunny or Pikachu they might actually be able to teach you gifts related to trickery or electricity, as they are quite likely to actually be proper standalone spirits due to the adoration of generations of kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T11:26:43-07:00","id":1488859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488793#post1488793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As humans creationss can be reflected in the umbra is there a limit? Cause some famous idea or concept, let's say star wars universe, could be be reflected somewhere in the umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like that won't appear in the Penumbra. But it could very well form somewhere in the Dream Zone where sub-realms that reflect human imagination can form. Garou could theoretically visit it, but few would. It's way in the Deep Umbra and probably has no relevance to the Garou except as a curiosity to some.<br /> <br /> Likewise, that doesn't mean you bring back a lightsaber from there or have Luke teach you a gift. That's getting silly. Such a lightsaber would only work in the particular confines of that segment of the Dream Zone. You can't bring it back to the physical realm because there isn't anything &quot;real&quot; that it is a part of. And any beings you meet there won't be spirits like you meet elsewhere. They are probably more like an Emanation. And such powers they have would only work in that specific realm of the Dream Zone since they're reflections of human imagination and NOT how the Gaian realm actually works. And even if they were, the means by which new spirits agree to teach Garou new gifts is more laborious than &quot;Yeah, you're cool so I'll tell you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T14:27:05-07:00","id":1488882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488859#post1488859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Likewise, that doesn't mean you bring back a lightsaber from there or have Luke teach you a gift. That's getting silly. Such a lightsaber would only work in the particular confines of that segment of the Dream Zone. You can't bring it back to the physical realm because there isn't anything &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; that it is a part of. And any beings you meet there won't be spirits like you meet elsewhere. They are probably more like an Emanation. And such powers they have would only work in that specific realm of the Dream Zone since they're reflections of human imagination and NOT how the Gaian realm actually works. And even if they were, the means by which new spirits agree to teach Garou new gifts is more laborious than &amp;quot;Yeah, you're cool so I'll tell you.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say silly, of course in those realm they are emanation but i agree with asmodai that the most famous would be powerfull enough to teach gift<br /> Even when you get out of the tv or cinema, what about religion? From the Garou knowledge and the world as it work in werewolf there's no god, only spirits, but the concept of god is so famous around the world that it surely has a reflection somewhere<br /> <br /> And where's the limit? If we talk about Cartoons or science fiction spirits they're just emanation and you cannot learn any power from them as you seems to tell, on the other hand we have some incarnae which has also been created by human mind and are not emanation at all (money incarnae named dollars for exemple)<br /> <br /> So true question, when is this just emanation and when is this true spiritual things/beings? Is there a law in some book that put a line or is ST the one that decide the final answer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T14:55:35-07:00","id":1488886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488882#post1488882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what about religion? From the Garou knowledge and the world as it work in werewolf there's no god, only spirits, but the concept of god is so famous around the world that it surely has a reflection somewhere</div> </div> </div> </div>This gets firmly into MtA territory, but you want to meet Hermes or Quetzalcoatl? Visit the right Spire in the High Umbra. Whether the entities you meet there are truly gods or the spiritual reflection of the concept of that god is up for debate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488882#post1488882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And where's the limit? If we talk about Cartoons or science fiction spirits they're just emanation and you cannot learn any power from them as you seems to tell, on the other hand we have some incarnae which has also been created by human mind and are not emanation at all (money incarnae named dollars for exemple)</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically for the ST to decide. If you decide that Wile E. Coyote is strong enough as a spiritual concept, sure, you can make him a proper Spirit that can hand out portable holes to Kakost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488882#post1488882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So true question, when is this just emanation and when is this true spiritual things/beings? Is there a law in some book that put a line or is ST the one that decide the final answer?</div> </div> </div> </div>No hard and fast rules. The ST decides, though the general guideline seems to be the older, bigger, and symbolically significant a concept or object is, the stronger the associated spirit. Really big concepts can become Realms or Zones (like the Dreaming).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T15:08:39-07:00","id":1488890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488882#post1488882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say silly, of course in those realm they are emanation but i agree with asmodai that the most famous would be powerfull enough to teach gift<br /> Even when you get out of the tv or cinema, what about religion? From the Garou knowledge and the world as it work in werewolf there's no god, only spirits, but the concept of god is so famous around the world that it surely has a reflection somewhere<br /> <br /> And where's the limit? If we talk about Cartoons or science fiction spirits they're just emanation and you cannot learn any power from them as you seems to tell, on the other hand we have some incarnae which has also been created by human mind and are not emanation at all (money incarnae named dollars for exemple)<br /> <br /> So true question, when is this just emanation and when is this true spiritual things/beings? Is there a law in some book that put a line or is ST the one that decide the final answer?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about how famous something is,but how long it was a part of someone's life and how much emotion is invested into it. I used Bugs Bunny as an example for the simple reason that for almost a 100 years he's been a part of people's childhoods and cultural touchstones in the west. Still, I doubt he is on the power level of a totem and would most likely be aligned with (ha!) Coyote, he is probably not very liked by the Garou. Most popular culture isn't on that level even with modern iconic fandoms. You need a long, long period of time for something to coalesce. The spirits you mentioned &quot;All Mighty Dollar&quot; and/or &quot;Easy Credit&quot; are Incarna that started in the conceptual realm, and with time and cultural worship of economy and prosperity grew into the spirits they are today. It's not something that happened just so, but a coalescence formed from the concept of the American Dream.<br /> <br /> The Far realms where dreams and hopes coalesce are not really something that has a lot of power and traction on its own, nor can it really interact well with the other Umbra, or the real world. They exist in and for themselves, with little comprehension of what actually is going on on the outside. So while I would posit that there may be entities there that are more powerful and could help you out or teach you something, I don't feel it's worthwhile taking the effort to meet them or to actually try and understand their ways enough that they would teach you gifts. I also imagine that anything that Bugs Bunny tries to teach you has a very good chance of killing you, simply because he wouldn't be able to understand your biology doesn't conform to cartoon physics.<br /> <br /> There are multiple things feeding on the concept that is organised abrahamic religion in Werewolf, the most likely thing you can point to is The Patriarch, a mighty Weaver spirit and representation of dogmatic organised religion.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of examples in the books of what makes a spirits powerful and what does not and we can discuss these examples, but at the end of the day the final arbiter will be the ST at the table. The TV Realms wouldn't be a place of powerful spirits with great impact on the world in my games, they could be crucial in yours.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T19:02:56-07:00","id":1488915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488882#post1488882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And where's the limit? If we talk about Cartoons or science fiction spirits they're just emanation and you cannot learn any power from them as you seems to tell, on the other hand we have some incarnae which has also been created by human mind and are not emanation at all (money incarnae named dollars for exemple)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also important to note that people don't think Star Wars is real. The setting is fictional. The characters in it are fictional. Its technology is fictional. People can love the stories, but everybody knows none of it is real.<br /> <br /> On the other hands, money is very real even though you can argue its a fictional concept that only exists because we believe it exists. Having a medium of exchange, unit of account, and store of value is a very useful thing. Whether it is based on some commodity or is fiat, people can see the money in their hand. And even as we head into the digital age where money is increasingly not something we physically have, but is a result of our credit or debit cards, they can see their value on some screen. Nobody ever acts like it is fake. Everybody acts as if it is real and meaningful. And have for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> Likewise if you start talking about the old pagan gods. While few believe in them now, at some point in the past you had thousands or millions of people truly believing in them for centuries and millennia. They just didn't think they were stories. People thought Zeus or Odin or Lugh were real. People prayed to them, sacrificed to them, built structures to them, devoted themselves to them in cults, etc. That is all significantly different behavior than even people performing cosplay, collecting memorabilia, and any other fan activity.<br /> <br /> What about things that children may believe are true, but adults don't? I think here you are approaching concepts better fit for Changeling, but obviously there can be some element of crossover in any setting. And traditionally the Werewolf game has chosen to treat such chimerical creatures as if they were spirits.<br /> <br /> To me, concepts that people know are fictional, would limit them to the imagination realms of the Dream Zone. Concepts that believe are real end up manifesting in the Astral Plane somehow, and some of these end up crossing over into the Middle Umbra which Garou can then theoretically contact. Exactly how Epiphlings, Weaver spirits, and their resultant Incarna are formed and interact is not laid out, so any ST will need to decide many things on their own.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T19:47:20-07:00","id":1488925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488833#post1488833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends on the type of Spirit. Most Spirits that inhabit a Realm are Emanations, a special type of Spirit that is created as part of the Realm itself. Technically, anything created within a Realm is an Emanation, including objects. While the Emanation of Superman may have super powers within its Realm, it does not have Charms or work at all like the Spirits you would encounter in the Spirit Wilds. A Luke Skywalker Emanation can't teach you to use the Force, at least not for outside its umbral bubble.<br /> <br /> If it helps, think of umbral Realms as Star Trek holodecks with the safety turned off. Emanations are everything the holodeck creates for its simulation. Once you change the simulation (step into another Realm, Zone, or the Penumbra), the rules change and anything you take with you has to follow those new rules. Once you leave the holodeck (cross the Gauntlet), stuff vanishes.<br /> <br /> I think there are certain Arts for Changelings that allow them to take things out of the Dreaming into the material world, but I'm pretty sure it's not that easy for Shapechangers. At least I can't think of a Gift on top of my head that would allow this.<br /> <br /> Rarely, there are physical objects that somehow found their way into umbral Realms and can be brought back. These tend to be fetishes or magic materials and are meant as quest goals- Pathstones are a good example.</div> </div> </div> </div>This work a bit differently for the Dreaming. In the Dreaming you can also pretty much everything that you can find in all the rest of the Umbra. But the Chimerae there can actually be brought to the physical world - and yes, you could, in theory, bring in Sauron's The One Ring to the physical world, the only thing you'd need (besides finding the LotR inside the Dreaming, finding the Chimerical Sauron and stealing from him - good luck) is calling the Wyrd, bringing the Dreaming temporarily to the material plane. There's also a few arts that allows them to materialize those.<br /> <br /> Bringing the Wyrd could also bring the Chimerae Superman in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T01:28:21-07:00","id":1488949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488915#post1488915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also important to note that people don't think Star Wars is real. The setting is fictional. The characters in it are fictional. Its technology is fictional. People can love the stories, but everybody knows none of it is real.<br /> <br /> On the other hands, money is very real even though you can argue its a fictional concept that only exists because we believe it exists. Having a medium of exchange, unit of account, and store of value is a very useful thing. Whether it is based on some commodity or is fiat, people can see the money in their hand. And even as we head into the digital age where money is increasingly not something we physically have, but is a result of our credit or debit cards, they can see their value on some screen. Nobody ever acts like it is fake. Everybody acts as if it is real and meaningful. And have for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> Likewise if you start talking about the old pagan gods. While few believe in them now, at some point in the past you had thousands or millions of people truly believing in them for centuries and millennia. They just didn't think they were stories. People thought Zeus or Odin or Lugh were real. People prayed to them, sacrificed to them, built structures to them, devoted themselves to them in cults, etc. That is all significantly different behavior than even people performing cosplay, collecting memorabilia, and any other fan activity.<br /> <br /> What about things that children may believe are true, but adults don't? I think here you are approaching concepts better fit for Changeling, but obviously there can be some element of crossover in any setting. And traditionally the Werewolf game has chosen to treat such chimerical creatures as if they were spirits.<br /> <br /> To me, concepts that people know are fictional, would limit them to the imagination realms of the Dream Zone. Concepts that believe are real end up manifesting in the Astral Plane somehow, and some of these end up crossing over into the Middle Umbra which Garou can then theoretically contact. Exactly how Epiphlings, Weaver spirits, and their resultant Incarna are formed and interact is not laid out, so any ST will need to decide many things on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you think that depending of our consideration the spiritual world will react differently? That's indeed an interesting point, i'm wandering what kind of reflection would give things that has existed but no longer now, you can still meet dinosaur in Pange if i remember, but what about some &quot;evil&quot; concept, is there a reflection somewhere in the umbra for racism spirits or worse (a certain kind of people known especially between 1939 and 1945 that could easily get an evil maybe wyrm spiritual reflection).<br /> <br /> You consider things that don't exist as emanation reflection but how does it work when it's something humanity want to forget, hate or prefer ignore but is famous and known for long enough to have a reflexion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T01:49:38-07:00","id":1488954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488949#post1488949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you think that depending of our consideration the spiritual world will react differently? That's indeed an interesting point, i'm wandering what kind of reflection would give things that has existed but no longer now, you can still meet dinosaur in Pange if i remember, but what about some &quot;evil&quot; concept, is there a reflection somewhere in the umbra for racism spirits or worse (a certain kind of people known especially between 1939 and 1945 that could easily get an evil maybe wyrm spiritual reflection).<br /> <br /> You consider things that don't exist as emanation reflection but how does it work when it's something humanity want to forget, hate or prefer ignore but is famous and known for long enough to have a reflexion?</div> </div> </div> </div>History, Emotion, Investment and thinking about things is what empowers them in the Umbra. Nazis have existed much longer than just 1939-1945, but considering the level of pain and trauma and weight they left (and are still leaving) on our world they exist in the Umbra as well. The realms they control or seek to conquer are horror shows of the worst excesses of fascist opression and genocide, and they repeat these actions ad nauseum. For instance, it could be a city under perpetual police hour, where scary black coated men-like things come and take you away to torture you into the night, it could be endless camps where emanations are murdered over and over again by more and more creative ideas, and it could be cold, lifeless nations where the absolute word of the ruler is truth and where anyone disagreeing dissapears. These realms would be some of the Wyrm's favourites and places where it might send its chosen to train. Heck it might even appoint someone to teach the spirits how to be even worse!<br /> <br /> There are actually sample realms like that, for instance the Fields of Wheat.<br /> <br /> If you want to forget something, that most likely has a bigger reflection than you want it to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T06:31:31-07:00","id":1488962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488949#post1488949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you think that depending of our consideration the spiritual world will react differently? That's indeed an interesting point, i'm wandering what kind of reflection would give things that has existed but no longer now, you can still meet dinosaur in Pange if i remember, but what about some &amp;quot;evil&amp;quot; concept, is there a reflection somewhere in the umbra for racism spirits or worse (a certain kind of people known especially between 1939 and 1945 that could easily get an evil maybe wyrm spiritual reflection).<br /> <br /> You consider things that don't exist as emanation reflection but how does it work when it's something humanity want to forget, hate or prefer ignore but is famous and known for long enough to have a reflexion?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll find all of those in the High Umbra, or Astral Plane, you'll find it in the Dreaming and you'll even find that in the Underworld, the so called Dark or Low Umbra, in the middle of the Tempest, in what wraiths call as a &quot;Far Shore&quot;. This &quot;Nazi Realm&quot; might even have a backdoor connecting it's different emanations of different portions of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Now, each one of those manifestations would have slighthly different collors. In the High Umbra, also called Astral Plane (I believe it's the Deep Umbra for WtA?) things would be more &quot;solid&quot;, since those would the <i>conceptual</i> spiritual reflection of what nazism was. So it would all look a lot more REAL, as if you had indeed entered Nazi German of the 1930's and 1940's, albeit in a much more Hollywoodian way. You probably wouldnt find a city or small german village that was basically unaffected - just remembering, there werent camps and bombs falling in every single inch of Germany, at least not until 1944-1945. Likewise, the spiritual reflections of WW2 would be more like Stalingrad or the famous &quot;Rape of Nanking&quot; (where the japanese massacred hundreds of thousands of chinese civilians, including doing unspeakable acts such empaling or boiling alive chinese BABIES - and yes, this happened, there's even pictures of it from japanese newspapers of the time). But wars are not like that; despite all the horrors, wars are 90% of the time made of absolutely boredom, where nothing happens except marching, moving hardware around, waiting for long, long hours of completely boredom for something to happen, and 10% of the time of the absolute onslaught and madness of the slaughterhouse. In the Astral reflection however, the entire war field will be much more like an endless Stalingrad or Nanking, just an endless and senseless slaughter non stop.<br /> <br /> In the Dreaming however, &quot;Nazi World&quot; would be the stuff of the nightmares. Instead of having spirits that look like humans in SS uniforms, those could appear as humanoid monstruosities, alien-like monsters without faces, without eyes or noses, and massive mouths with shark-like sharp theets, dressed in the same SS uniforms. Anything to inspire fear. Just imagine what would be like to be having a nightmare about nazis, instead of a clear visualization of them. Thus, any kind of &quot;Cthulhu-esq&quot; depiction of them would be good to go<br /> <br /> In the Underworld, Dark or Low Umbra, they would be also more nightmarish than in the Astral Plane, but less fantastic and alien than in the Dreaming, and more &quot;Death-Like&quot;. The prisoners in the camps would be like walking corpses, the plasmic SS Nazis would look like twisted humans (perhaps with repulsive deformations, such as skins like nosferatu vampires) than xenomorph horror aliens such as in the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T06:56:58-07:00","id":1488967,"title":"","content":"The Low Umbra, if you use Wraith's geography for it, really doesn't have a specific realm for anything. Instead you'd have the ghostly relics of specific destroyed objects and locations incorporated into the local Necropoli (ghostly communities in penumbral cities) and Byways (relatively safe pathways in the Tempest). There are no spiritual representations of the Nazis in the Underworld, but there are the ghosts of actual Nazis there, especially amongst the ranks of the Spectres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T07:06:05-07:00","id":1488968,"title":"","content":"The Low Umbra or Dark Umbra has a penumbral area, the Shadowlands, but it also has areas not specifically tied to co-inside with material places. Everything within the Tempest is removed from the material world, be it areas like Stygia, or even farther away, the Far Shore (which represent the Heavens and Hells of various believes). So, that are kind of specific realms within the Low or Dark Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T07:11:22-07:00","id":1488969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488967#post1488967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Low Umbra, if you use Wraith's geography for it, really doesn't have a specific realm for anything. Instead you'd have the ghostly relics of specific destroyed objects and locations incorporated into the local Necropoli (ghostly communities in penumbral cities) and Byways (relatively safe pathways in the Tempest). There are no spiritual representations of the Nazis in the Underworld, but there are the ghosts of actual Nazis there, especially amongst the ranks of the Spectres.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about the Far Shores? Those arent just the &quot;ghost towns&quot; of ages passed, but rather mythical lands","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T08:13:09-07:00","id":1488976,"title":"","content":"The Far Shores are islands in the Tempest, much like Stygia. Their primary purpose was as waystations for Wraiths to seek Transcendence so many of them were themed after the afterlives of various religions, but they were not meant to actually be representative of those afterlives or beliefs. It's not entirely clear how they sprang into existence, but the Shining Ones who ran them were actual Wraiths which is why many fell to their shadows and became Spectres. <br /> <br /> It is possible that before the Tempest washed away most of the Low Umbra there were more coherent realms, and that the byways and pockets of safety are just the remnants of them. That time is long gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T09:47:36-07:00","id":1488980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488976#post1488976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Far Shores are islands in the Tempest, much like Stygia. Their primary purpose was as waystations for Wraiths to seek Transcendence so many of them were themed after the afterlives of various religions, but they were not meant to actually be representative of those afterlives or beliefs. It's not entirely clear how they sprang into existence, but the Shining Ones who ran them were actual Wraiths which is why many fell to their shadows and became Spectres. <br /> <br /> It is possible that before the Tempest washed away most of the Low Umbra there were more coherent realms, and that the byways and pockets of safety are just the remnants of them. That time is long gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I always thought both the Tempest and the Labyrinth were more like &quot;theater of the mind&quot; places; also, if they can have places like Asgard, Olympus and Gehenna or Nifelheim, I thought that perhaps the human collective minds had more of a pull on what could appear down there. I mean, I would understand fully destroted cities in there or even fully &quot;new&quot; cities otherwise built by the dead such as Stygia, but not mythical places like the Celestial Bureocracy, unless other things showed up too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T10:04:21-07:00","id":1488985,"title":"","content":"Anyway the more we think about it the more it seems to be entirely up to the ST to decide what will be simple emanations and what will be true spirit to interract with.<br /> I thougt about war, it's a human (or at least a consciousness being) concept, very real, and has many reflection in the umbra (battleground to quote only that) but there are also war spirits that can be emanations of the war concept, and yet they can teach gift to garou and serve into fetishe without being specific reflexion of someone. War spirit as described seems to be incarnation of war under a form or another but the book never state what they look like when you meet them. We can assume that war spirit could take the form of a soldier, a warrior, a weapon or anything that can in his form embody war. <br /> <br /> So if the ST feel like if you meet an orc of sauron it can teach gifts then he could describe it the same way he would describe Jagglins in comparison of Gafflins, no?<br /> Of course it's but a theorie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 08-03-2022, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T11:03:43-07:00","id":1488994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488980#post1488980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm... I always thought both the Tempest and the Labyrinth were more like &quot;theater of the mind&quot; places; also, if they can have places like Asgard, Olympus and Gehenna or Nifelheim, I thought that perhaps the human collective minds had more of a pull on what could appear down there. I mean, I would understand fully destroted cities in there or even fully &quot;new&quot; cities otherwise built by the dead such as Stygia, but not mythical places like the Celestial Bureocracy, unless other things showed up too</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Human minds have as much pull on the Low Umbra as on the other Umbras. However each of the Umbrae is a different facet of the mind and for the Low Umbra that facet is memory. Relics are the memories of places and objects, Wraiths are, in some ways, the memories of people. You can even argue (and I often do) that much of the substance of the Tempest and the Labyrinth is made up of memories, fragmented memories and suppressed memories respectively. <br /> <br /> In that sense, elements of WWII will show up in the Underworld, but they aren't going to be coherent realms. The Tempest may sometimes throw up rains of shrapnel, barbed wire, and ashes, for instance. There will be halls in the Labyrinth that will be bunkers from the front lines or [insert imagery I don't care to describe] from the camps. Distinct cities and zones, though, tend to be made by Wraiths or Spectres.<br /> <br /> Gods and afterlives, even those having to do with death (like Hades and, well, Hades) are the stuff of the High Umbra and they will show up there. There are elements of myth and legend that show up in the Low Umbra, but usually in mysterious and undefined ways. Anubis and the Lady of Fate show up in the Underworld, for instance, but we don't actually know what they are. They could be anything from monumentally old Wraiths (the Lady might be Eve, for instance) to things from outside the Underworld. <br /> <br /> None of this is meant to limit you from putting something like Valhalla or Tartarus in the Underworld, just to point out that the structure of that Umbra doesn't lend itself in that direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T13:21:40-07:00","id":1489006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488985#post1488985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway the more we think about it the more it seems to be entirely up to the ST to decide what will be simple emanations and what will be true spirit to interract with.<br /> I thougt about war, it's a human (or at least a consciousness being) concept, very real, and has many reflection in the umbra (battleground to quote only that) but there are also war spirits that can be emanations of the war concept, and yet they can teach gift to garou and serve into fetishe without being specific reflexion of someone. War spirit as described seems to be incarnation of war under a form or another but the book never state what they look like when you meet them. We can assume that war spirit could take the form of a soldier, a warrior, a weapon or anything that can in his form embody war.<br /> <br /> So if the ST feel like if you meet an orc of sauron it can teach gifts then he could describe it the same way he would describe Jagglins in comparison of Gafflins, no?<br /> Of course it's but a theorie</div> </div> </div> </div>War is an ancient concept that has defined human interactions since before we became human, are you actually surprised that it would have a whole gamut of spirits? From the least sparks of conflict to the glorious Gods of the Great Wars?<br /> <br /> While it's correct it's down to the ST to decide what is and is not an emanation, there are some quite clear guidelines on what an emanation is and isn't. To understand them you need to realise that realms are essentially perpetual plays persisting a storyline and narrative they resonate with - emanations are the actors of these plays, repeating them over and over. They are less independant spirits and more moving parts that makes the realm what it is. And that's why their power is define by the realm they belong to.<br /> <br /> Now, in a Realm there can also be actually spirits who may be mixed in, these would probably be vastly more powerful and relevant than he echoes of the story the Realm is perpetuating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488994#post1488994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human minds have as much pull on the Low Umbra as on the other Umbras. However each of the Umbrae is a different facet of the mind and for the Low Umbra that facet is memory. Relics are the memories of places and objects, Wraiths are, in some ways, the memories of people. You can even argue (and I often do) that much of the substance of the Tempest and the Labyrinth is made up of memories, fragmented memories and suppressed memories respectively.<br /> <br /> In that sense, elements of WWII will show up in the Underworld, but they aren't going to be coherent realms. The Tempest may sometimes throw up rains of shrapnel, barbed wire, and ashes, for instance. There will be halls in the Labyrinth that will be bunkers from the front lines or [insert imagery I don't care to describe] from the camps. Distinct cities and zones, though, tend to be made by Wraiths or Spectres.<br /> <br /> Gods and afterlives, even those having to do with death (like Hades and, well, Hades) are the stuff of the High Umbra and they will show up there. There are elements of myth and legend that show up in the Low Umbra, but usually in mysterious and undefined ways. Anubis and the Lady of Fate show up in the Underworld, for instance, but we don't actually know what they are. They could be anything from monumentally old Wraiths (the Lady might be Eve, for instance) to things from outside the Underworld.<br /> <br /> None of this is meant to limit you from putting something like Valhalla or Tartarus in the Underworld, just to point out that the structure of that Umbra doesn't lend itself in that direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to second this. In general the afterlives of myth and religion are found in the Umbra, not in the Dark Umbra. The Dark Umbra seems to be even more anthropocentric than the regular one and built on memories and longing. As for where souls go, is a whole other question, and it seems that they go to many different places, and that both umbral realms and the shadelands may just be waypoints for certain souls before they go where they are meant to.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T14:26:30-07:00","id":1489015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488994#post1488994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Human minds have as much pull on the Low Umbra as on the other Umbras. However each of the Umbrae is a different facet of the mind and for the Low Umbra that facet is memory. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating! I never though about it that way!<br /> <br /> By that analogy, we could even say the High Umbra (or Deep Umbra or Astral Plane) is the part of the &quot;mind of the universe&quot; that is related to abstraction and cognition, the Dreaming would be imagination and the middle Umbra would be related to our senses (sight, hearing etc). That's also!<br /> <br /> We could even go so far as to say that the Tellurium is &quot;God's Mind&quot;.<br /> <br /> I loved that analogy, I think I'll structure the entire cosmology based on the human mind.<br /> <br /> Now I wonder: could it be that this is what the writers did? Subconciously (or perhaps on purpose) modeled the cosmology based on the human mind?<br /> <br /> This opens up many possibilities: Oblivion could just be the process by which our minds &quot;erase&quot; old, useless memories. The Abyss could work as the archtypical Jungian &quot;Shadow&quot;, the self destructive portion of our minds. &quot;Gaia&quot; could be the &quot;Anima&quot;, the female portion of a male's mind (now I need to find what could constitute the &quot;Animus&quot;, the male conterpart of a female). The Wyld could be &quot;God's Id&quot;, the Weaver could be the Superego, and the Wyrm is.... the Ego. Which... Tragically indicate that God is... Sick in the &quot;head&quot;. And literally adopting self destructive behaviors.<br /> <br /> Sometime ago, I was seeking to fuse Demon the Fallen with Mage lore, so Lucifer believed that humanity had within them the power to defeat God, if properly guided.<br /> <br /> What I decided is that... Humanity <b>have God inside of them</b>. Adding Mage lore, each Avatar is a shard of The One. <br /> <br /> Thus, in my personal headcanon, God literally &quot;sacrificed himself for us&quot;. But now... I'll add a little twist.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;God&quot; is the entire Tellurian. The &quot;God&quot; that Lucifer knew was his AVATAR (not in Mage terms, but rather the hinduistic terms aka the physical manifestation of a divine being).<br /> <br /> Thus, this one almight entity DIED (of course, because the Tellurian still exists), and his &quot;essence&quot; got fragmented into infinity pieces - the Avatars from Mage.<br /> <br /> All this is gonna be wonderful for my Dreamspeakers, since in my game they only have 3 Spheres, Spirit, Mind and Body, representing the 3 pieces of &quot;the Dream&quot; that is the creation. So, modeling the entire cosmology on the human mind, it means that the &quot;primitives&quot; are the ones closer to the truth hehe<br /> <br /> I loved that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T14:39:01-07:00","id":1489017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1488994#post1488994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Human minds have as much pull on the Low Umbra as on the other Umbras. However each of the Umbrae is a different facet of the mind and for the Low Umbra that facet is memory. Relics are the memories of places and objects, Wraiths are, in some ways, the memories of people. You can even argue (and I often do) that much of the substance of the Tempest and the Labyrinth is made up of memories, fragmented memories and suppressed memories respectively. <br /> <br /> In that sense, elements of WWII will show up in the Underworld, but they aren't going to be coherent realms. The Tempest may sometimes throw up rains of shrapnel, barbed wire, and ashes, for instance. There will be halls in the Labyrinth that will be bunkers from the front lines or [insert imagery I don't care to describe] from the camps. Distinct cities and zones, though, tend to be made by Wraiths or Spectres.<br /> <br /> Gods and afterlives, even those having to do with death (like Hades and, well, Hades) are the stuff of the High Umbra and they will show up there. There are elements of myth and legend that show up in the Low Umbra, but usually in mysterious and undefined ways. Anubis and the Lady of Fate show up in the Underworld, for instance, but we don't actually know what they are. They could be anything from monumentally old Wraiths (the Lady might be Eve, for instance) to things from outside the Underworld. <br /> <br /> None of this is meant to limit you from putting something like Valhalla or Tartarus in the Underworld, just to point out that the structure of that Umbra doesn't lend itself in that direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, one of the hard things about WoD - and also a great bonus to it, in my opinion - is that some things are hard to define in a chicken-egg situation. For example, Anubis exists in the Underworld. Is he an almighty ghost or something out of the Underworld? We do not know. So, did the Anubis that exists in the Underworld created the mortal myths in Egypt - or the egyptian myths eventually created a powerful Spirit that ended up taking residence into the Underworld, coming from the Astral Plane or the Dreaming? We do not know, and we have no way of knowing. Either option could be true. He could be a powerful Chimerae &quot;born&quot; out of human imagination, that increased in power over the centuries, and eventually settled in the Underworld. Or he could a mighty Wraith, thus he would be the cause of the legends, not the consequence. <br /> <br /> And this possibilities are fantastic. For example, you may find Odin in the Astral Plane. Is this entity a powerful spirit that was born out of centuries of human worship, or is he something entirely different (a Firstborn Fae perhaps? Something else?) that played on Earth for long enough to have the nordic mortals start worshipping him?<br /> <br /> Do all those &quot;gods&quot; were creations of humans, or they are the ones responsible for the legends to exist? Maybe some are one, and others another?<br /> <br /> There's no way to know, and that's awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T01:44:38-07:00","id":1489070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489015#post1489015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fascinating! I never though about it that way!<br /> <br /> By that analogy, we could even say the High Umbra (or Deep Umbra or Astral Plane) is the part of the &quot;mind of the universe&quot; that is related to abstraction and cognition, the Dreaming would be imagination and the middle Umbra would be related to our senses (sight, hearing etc). That's also!<br /> <br /> We could even go so far as to say that the Tellurium is &quot;God's Mind&quot;.<br /> <br /> I loved that analogy, I think I'll structure the entire cosmology based on the human mind.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Personnally even if i understand why you like that analogy, i prefer the one that the umbra react to it but isn't entirely shaped by human mind, cause one of the theme of WTA is that human aren't any special in comparison of other beings. If you play Mage the Ascension and base your story on it, then it fit that idea, not really in werewolf where the universe is shaped by the triat. However human mind contribute to some changes and transformations but with spirits and the Wyld, i don't think humans are the main factor to the umbra alteration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T02:05:42-07:00","id":1489074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489070#post1489070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However human mind contribute to some changes and transformations but with spirits and the Wyld, i don't think humans are the main factor to the umbra alteration</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a clever little feedback loop between conscious beings of the material world and Spirits in the Umbra. Even Sleepers can be influenced by active Spirits who by their nature want to nurture their aspects, and in return conscious beings shape more of the Umbra. Humans are of course not the only ones involved in this process, but far and away the main contributors, by virtue of their number and level of consciousness. The books repeatedly make it clear that humanity has been fostered by the Triat for that role. Any change is therefore a dual process between material and spirit world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T05:13:26-07:00","id":1489095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489070#post1489070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personnally even if i understand why you like that analogy, i prefer the one that the umbra react to it but isn't entirely shaped by human mind, cause one of the theme of WTA is that human aren't any special in comparison of other beings. If you play Mage the Ascension and base your story on it, then it fit that idea, not really in werewolf where the universe is shaped by the triat. However human mind contribute to some changes and transformations but with spirits and the Wyld, i don't think humans are the main factor to the umbra alteration</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you got me wrong, I didnt mean that HUMANITY is what shapes the cosmology, Im not saying that HUMANS are what define reality, Im saying that the Tellurian exists as a CONCIOUS BEING. Hence having an structure that ressembles how a brain works - memory, pleasure, creativity, senses, etc etc etc. It's still compatible with either Werewolf or Mage, it's just a matter of how you wanna look to it. Like I said, the Triad could be the &quot;Ego, Superego and Id&quot; of the Tellurian, and yes those would still be the forming forces of the universe's &quot;mind&quot; and that has nothing to do with humanity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T06:23:22-07:00","id":1489102,"title":"","content":"You may enjoy the hermetic concept of <a href=\"https://religion.fandom.com/wiki/The_All\" target=\"_blank\">The All</a>, and by extension <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Kybalion\" target=\"_blank\">The Kybalion</a> as a non-game source for these ideas.<br /> <br /> As for whether or not this was intentional by the authors, the answer is probably yesn't. Since they took a whole lot of existing esoteric ideas to build the WoD around, some deeper considerations carry over naturally. The Triat for example is the classic triplicity Cardinal, Mutable, Fixed which exists as concept under many guises (Mind, Body, Soul) in plenty of philosophical and esoteric concepts. But as a Mage player, you already know a thing or two about correspondences.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T10:19:41-07:00","id":1489129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489095#post1489095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, you got me wrong, I didnt mean that HUMANITY is what shapes the cosmology, Im not saying that HUMANS are what define reality, Im saying that the Tellurian exists as a CONCIOUS BEING. Hence having an structure that ressembles how a brain works - memory, pleasure, creativity, senses, etc etc etc. It's still compatible with either Werewolf or Mage, it's just a matter of how you wanna look to it. Like I said, the Triad could be the &amp;quot;Ego, Superego and Id&amp;quot; of the Tellurian, and yes those would still be the forming forces of the universe's &amp;quot;mind&amp;quot; and that has nothing to do with humanity</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops, sorry bad translation, my bad x) still an very interesting point of view anyway<br /> <br /> Now maybe i missed something but does any book say how much the alteration in the penumbra will affect the pysical world? The book give the exemple of a tree, of cut in the umbra it's r\u00e9flexion will. We can assume it can take hours or maybe days but what with stronger alteration? Earthquake, tsunami (atomic bomb) etc that provoque big transformation in the environnement for long time? Does one affect the other immediately if the alteration is strong enough or will it take some time to adapt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T10:23:08-07:00","id":1489131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489102#post1489102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may enjoy the hermetic concept of <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://religion.fandom.com/wiki/The_All&amp;quot;]The</a> All[/URL], and by extension <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Kybalion&amp;quot;]The</a> Kybalion[/URL] as a non-game source for these ideas.<br /> <br /> As for whether or not this was intentional by the authors, the answer is probably yesn't. Since they took a whole lot of existing esoteric ideas to build the WoD around, some deeper considerations carry over naturally. The Triat for example is the classic triplicity Cardinal, Mutable, Fixed which exists as concept under many guises (Mind, Body, Soul) in plenty of philosophical and esoteric concepts. But as a Mage player, you already know a thing or two about correspondences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>The Seven Hermetic Principles</b><br /> 1. The principle of mentalism<br /> <br /> &quot;The All is Mind; the Universe is Mental.&quot;[5]<br /> <br /> 2. The principle of correspondence<br /> <br /> &quot;As above, so below; as below, so above.\u201d [...] This principle embodies the truth that there is always a correspondence between the laws and phenomena of the various planes of being and life.[6]<br /> <br /> 3. The principle of vibration<br /> <br /> &quot;Nothing rests; everything moves; everything vibrates.&quot;[7]<br /> <br /> 4. The principle of polarity<br /> <br /> &quot;Everything is dual; everything has poles; everything has its pair of opposites; like and unlike are the same; opposites are identical in nature, but different in degree; extremes meet; all truths are but half-truths; all paradoxes may be reconciled.&quot;[8]<br /> <br /> 5. The principle of rhythm<br /> <br /> &quot;Everything flows, out and in; everything has its tides; all things rise and fall; the pendulum-swing manifests in everything; the measure of the swing to the right is the measure of the swing to the left; rhythm compensates.&quot;[9]<br /> <br /> 6. The principle of cause and effect<br /> <br /> &quot;Every cause has its effect; every effect has its cause; everything happens according to law; chance is but a name for law not recognized; there are many planes of causation, but nothing escapes the law.&quot;[10]<br /> <br /> 7. The principle of gender<br /> <br /> &quot;Gender is in everything; everything has its masculine and feminine principles; gender manifests on all planes.&quot;[11]<br /> <br /> Yes yes, that's very good... Im looking towards a &quot;unified field&quot; for all &quot;magical theory&quot; on the WoD, that could give a &quot;universal cosmogy&quot;, that could encompass ALL the theories, both from all the different magic currents but also from the non human beings (fera, vamps, changellings, wraiths, fallen, spirits). This helps a lot, thank you very much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T12:32:47-07:00","id":1489143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489131#post1489131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im looking towards a &quot;unified field&quot; for all &quot;magical theory&quot; on the WoD, that could give a &quot;universal cosmogy&quot;, that could encompass ALL the theories, both from all the different magic currents but also from the non human beings (fera, vamps, changellings, wraiths, fallen, spirits). This helps a lot, thank you very much</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, keep in mind this is just the (fairly modern) hermetic view on things. Remember the &quot;Elephant and the Blind Men&quot;. Good luck!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489129#post1489129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now maybe i missed something but does any book say how much the alteration in the penumbra will affect the pysical world? The book give the exemple of a tree, of cut in the umbra it's r\u00e9flexion will. We can assume it can take hours or maybe days but what with stronger alteration? Earthquake, tsunami (atomic bomb) etc that provoque big transformation in the environnement for long time? Does one affect the other immediately if the alteration is strong enough or will it take some time to adapt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, no hard rules, and it depends on both the change and the circumstances. There is much more symbolism involved than direct cause and effect, though. If you cut down a sacred tree with a powerful spirit, it might slowly wither away in the Penumbra instead of just vanishing. If you demolish a home beloved by its tenants, it may just as quickly disappear in the Penumbra but might pop up in the Shadowlands instead. If a concept gets disavowed by the larger public, its Realm may crumble or rot.<br /> <br /> As aside, setting off nukes has proven to be a very bad idea, especially within the Umbra.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T14:04:26-07:00","id":1489150,"title":"","content":"Hermetic thought is really something that doesn't go well with W:tA, in character or out. Out of character, it's really irritating to play the game &quot;ironically&quot; as if none of the setting really exists outside of, say, the will of the Garou. In-character, you run into problems when most Garou and Fera snick the offenders in-universe who suggest that, say, their ancestor spirits are just figments of their imagination. And if it doesn't do well for W:tA, it really doesn't do well for the Middle Umbra, either (and probably not other Umbrae, but definitely not for Werewolf's stomping grounds).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T14:55:52-07:00","id":1489158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489150#post1489150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hermetic thought is really something that doesn't go well with W:tA, in character or out. Out of character, it's really irritating to play the game &quot;ironically&quot; as if none of the setting really exists outside of, say, the will of the Garou. In-character, you run into problems when most Garou and Fera snick the offenders in-universe who suggest that, say, their ancestor spirits are just figments of their imagination. And if it doesn't do well for W:tA, it really doesn't do well for the Middle Umbra, either (and probably not other Umbrae, but definitely not for Werewolf's stomping grounds).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that is perhaps a bit of a misinterpretation. &quot;The Universe is Mental&quot; does not mean that it is the product of individual minds, it means that material reality is the surface of a body that is <i>not</i> material. It's closer to the idea of the Holographic Universe, if you want a physical analogy. To quote the book directly:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The All is infinite living mind - the illuminated call it Spirit </div> </div> </div>So basically, underneath the thin material layer exists the spiritual layer, and the whole of it is a thing with agency. That goes actually pretty well with the Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean it's the only or best way to look at a Werewolf's world, of course. The animistic view of &quot;a bird can fly, because it is the nature of birds to fly&quot; is just as valid and in most cases works even better because the WtA world is built upon animistic principles.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T15:25:58-07:00","id":1489160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489150#post1489150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hermetic thought is really something that doesn't go well with W:tA, in character or out. Out of character, it's really irritating to play the game &amp;quot;ironically&amp;quot; as if none of the setting really exists outside of, say, the will of the Garou. In-character, you run into problems when most Garou and Fera snick the offenders in-universe who suggest that, say, their ancestor spirits are just figments of their imagination. And if it doesn't do well for W:tA, it really doesn't do well for the Middle Umbra, either (and probably not other Umbrae, but definitely not for Werewolf's stomping grounds).</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I was imagining, the middle Umbra could represent our SENSES in this analogy, which is why everything is so much more... &quot;Solid&quot; in it, or more &quot;real&quot; (as compared to the weird abstractions of the Astral Plane or the surreal stuff of the Dreaming). Thus, the Middle Umbra wouldnt represent what &quot;God&quot; (or the &quot;mind&quot; or &quot;spirit&quot; of the Tellurian) imagines or what his cognition/abstractions think, but rather what this &quot;universal mind&quot; <i>percieves</i>.<br /> <br /> Even Hermetic thought doesnt describe all too way the WoD, since this is not a solypsistic universe, but more of a Deistic one like hinduism upon which everything is Vishnu's dream or Barkeley's immaterialism.<br /> If we go to the notion that Avatars are &quot;Shards of the One&quot; than... Well, yeah, CONSENSUS is basically that, the reflection of &quot;God&quot; or the &quot;Tellurian's&quot; will.<br /> <br /> So, things are NOT a reflection of the werewolf's mind, it's not an allucination of his. Things ARE. But at the same time, the Tellurian itself is a living, and intelligent or even concious, being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T15:28:37-07:00","id":1489161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489158#post1489158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, that is perhaps a bit of a misinterpretation. &amp;quot;The Universe is Mental&amp;quot; does not mean that it is the product of individual minds, it means that material reality is the surface of a body that is <i>not</i> material. It's closer to the idea of the Holographic Universe, if you want a physical analogy. To quote the book directly:<br /> So basically, underneath the thin material layer exists the spiritual layer, and the whole of it is a thing with agency. That goes actually pretty well with the Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean it's the only or best way to look at a Werewolf's world, of course. The animistic view of &amp;quot;a bird can fly, because it is the nature of birds to fly&amp;quot; is just as valid and in most cases works even better because the WtA world is built upon animistic principles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Ultimately, WtA and MtA cosmologies are irreconciable. That's what I would like to fix, and create the &quot;Unified Spiritual Field&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T17:14:58-07:00","id":1489169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489161#post1489161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. Ultimately, WtA and MtA cosmologies are irreconciable. That's what I would like to fix, and create the &quot;Unified Spiritual Field&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a problem, and it doesn't need fixing. It allows vastly different games to explore extremely different thematic spaces, as their needs are not all the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T20:02:44-07:00","id":1489180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489169#post1489169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a problem, and it doesn't need fixing. It allows vastly different games to explore extremely different thematic spaces, as their needs are not all the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok pal, Im not forcing anybody to take my ideas, Im just simply brainstorming random stuff to the winds, if anybody likes em cool, if not cool too. I just found it a fascinating idea to think on the spirit world as a living entity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T01:18:13-07:00","id":1489200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489169#post1489169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a problem, and it doesn't need fixing. It allows vastly different games to explore extremely different thematic spaces, as their needs are not all the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hear, hear!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488772-the-true-potential-of-the-umbra?p=1489180#post1489180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok pal, Im not forcing anybody to take my ideas, Im just simply brainstorming random stuff to the winds, if anybody likes em cool, if not cool too. I just found it a fascinating idea to think on the spirit world as a living entity</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's more about that your ideas can be fun for you and your game, but we're kinda used to people trying to squeeze everything in no matter what it messes up with the games themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}